Subject: [PATCH 37/37] replay1017-v0163.0: re-pin the lock, identity and crate
 metadata to rust-v0.163.0

The 36-commit replay carried the rust-v0.159.2 lockfile and upstream
identity across verbatim. Rebase the lock file onto upstream's official
0.163.0 lock instead of hand-merging it:

- base: upstream rust-v0.163.0 codex-rs/Cargo.lock
  (sha256 17cdd862471774ba7aef836aaf0a0a3ed76bd23e503b1fc7278c89d1f2719d03)
- add the codex-transportd workspace package entry
- normalise the 160 local workspace packages 0.0.0 -> 0.163.0
  (same convention as the 0.159.2 line; cargo accepts it under --locked)
- stale 0.159.2-only packages drop out with upstream:
  codex-shell-escalation, proc-macro-error2, proc-macro-error-attr2
- 0.163.0-only packages come in with upstream:
  codex-cloud-client, codex-windows-sandbox-test-support, file-id, hpke,
  linkify, proc-macro-error3, proc-macro-error-attr3, rand_pcg

Verified:
  cargo metadata --locked --offline  -> exit 0
  lock sha256 = d4f528484ecb085fcedf7b212349f18b8b009566ed0033177be2fbb4f6c0e3d9

Identity strings re-pinned in the same commit so the evidence commit below
stays confined to the replay gate's evidence allowlist:
build_info.rs (tag/peeled commit/lock/toolchain), crate description,
Dockerfile default RELEASE_ID, and the two module doc comments that name
the official baseline. Toolchain stays 1.95.0.
